{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1315637744/7/codegen_prompts/3.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1315637744/7`\n- 题号：`3`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1315637744/7/3.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"3\">\n- `description`：将散落的碎片对象拼入与其形状匹配的模板槽位中，拼入后碎片的颜色由槽位边框上的标记色决定。\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 black。\n  - 网格中央有一个由 grey 构成的大矩形模板框架，框架内有若干个形状各异的镂空槽位（槽位内为 black）。\n  - 每个槽位的边框上恰好有一个非 grey、非 black 的单像素标记点（如 red、blue、green 等），该标记点位于槽位边缘的 grey 像素中。\n  - 模板外部散落着若干单色碎片对象（颜色统一为 maroon），每个碎片的形状恰好与某个槽位的形状完全吻合（经过平移，不旋转不翻转）。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 将每个 maroon 碎片与形状完全匹配的槽位配对（一一对应）。\n  - 将碎片平移到对应槽位的位置，填入槽位。\n  - 填入后，碎片的颜色不保留 maroon，而是变为该槽位边框上标记点的颜色。\n  - 模板框架（grey）和标记点保持不变；碎片原位置清除为 black。\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要完成三层推理——第一层是形状匹配（识别碎片与哪个槽位吻合），第二层是发现槽位边框上存在颜色标记，第三层是发现填入后的颜色取自该标记而非碎片原色。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：eval/dfadab01, train/99caaf76, eval/247ef758, train/afe3afe9, eval/2c181942, train/46c35fc7, eval/edb79dae, train/9f669b64\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"dfadab01\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3798\nmechanism=0.5079\nlexical=0.0224\ncode_feature=0.2500\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:marker, object:sprite, object:template, operation:translate, relation:direction\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/dfadab01.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/dfadab01.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nExpand each colored control pixel into its corresponding fixed 4x4 glyph.\n\nInput structure:\n- Black background with single-pixel markers in colors 2, 3, 5, and/or 8.\n- Some inputs also show a sample 4x4 glyph in the output color, with a same-rule marker just below-right of the sample.\n\nRule:\n- Replace each marker color by its learned 4x4 glyph: 2->yellow frame, 3->blue ring, 5->pink diagonal blocks, 8->orange X.\n- Paint each glyph with its top-left corner at the marker pixel, clipping at the grid boundary.\n- Remove the sample glyphs and skip their below-right label markers.\n\nKey insight:\n- The colored pixels are control pixels for a fixed glyph alphabet; non-control sample glyphs are only legend entries, not preserved scene objects.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"single-pixel markers in the glyph alphabet colors\",\n  \"transform\": \"replace each marker by its fixed 4x4 glyph, clipped at grid edge; sample glyphs and their below-right labels disappear\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"99caaf76\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3536\nmechanism=0.4262\nlexical=0.0190\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:rotation, object:grid_edge, object:marker, object:sprite, operation:rotate, operation:translate, output:same_size, relation:direction\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/99caaf76.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/99caaf76.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nMove each marked cross object away from its marker to the grid edge while rotating the colored cross 180 degrees.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- Each 8-connected foreground object has nine pixels: a 4-pixel marker-color\n  sprite attached to a 5-pixel non-marker colored cross.\n- Each object bbox is either 3x6 or 6x3, so the marker sprite is on exactly\n  one side of the cross.\n\nRule:\n- Move the whole object straight away from its marker side until the object\n  bbox touches the corresponding grid edge.\n- Keep the marker sprite unchanged within the object.\n- Rotate the 3x3 colored cross block by 180 degrees before placing it.\n\nKey insight:\nThe marker sprite is a directional tail; the cross is the leading payload,\nand only that payload turns around during the slide to the edge.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"each 8-connected composite object made of a 4-pixel blue marker sprite attached to a 5-pixel colored cross\",\n  \"path\": \"straight away from the marker sprite until the composite bbox reaches the grid edge\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"move the whole composite rigidly along that path\",\n  \"transform\": \"rotate the 3x3 colored cross 180 degrees within the composite; keep the marker sprite unchanged\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"247ef758\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3561\nmechanism=0.4603\nlexical=0.0158\ncode_feature=0.3333\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:marker, object:rectangle, object:sprite, operation:translate, relation:direction\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/247ef758.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/247ef758.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nMove colored sprites from the left strip into a framed area at marker-defined targets.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg background; rectangular frame on right with colored markers on its edges; sprites in a narrow left strip separated by a constant-color divider column.\n\nRule:\n- For each color, target rows/cols are where both opposite frame edges share that color. Targets are the Cartesian product.\n- Erase each sprite from the left and stamp it centered at every target. Higher sprites cover lower ones.\n\nKey insight: One sprite replicates to a grid of row × column marker intersections.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"sprite s in the left area whose color appears on the right frame\",\n  \"dst\": \"center at positions d in the right frame\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.color == d.same_row_frame_edges.color and s.color == d.same_col_frame_edges.color\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"move sprites from bottom to top, with new covering old\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"afe3afe9\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3664\nmechanism=0.4632\nlexical=0.0175\ncode_feature=0.4000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:marker, object:sprite, operation:rotate, operation:translate, relation:direction\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/afe3afe9.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/afe3afe9.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nConvert each hollow 3x3 symbol to one pixel and slide the pixels clockwise from the marked edge.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has a background, one full-edge marker line, and monochrome hollow 3x3 foreground symbols.\n- The symbols lie on a coarse row/column lattice; fully empty lattice rows or columns are absent from the output.\n\nRule\n- Replace each hollow 3x3 symbol with one pixel of its color in the corresponding coarse-grid cell.\n- The marker edge gives the compaction direction by clockwise border travel: top -> right, right -> down, bottom -> left, left -> up.\n- Preserve the order of non-background pixels while sliding them as far as possible in that direction.\n\nKey insight\n- The large picture is a scaled symbolic grid, and the blue edge marker acts as a gravity direction rather than as output content.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"hollow 3x3 foreground symbols collapsed to one coarse-grid pixel each; the full-edge blue marker selects the path direction\",\n  \"path\": \"straight along each coarse row or column in clockwise border direction from the marker edge: top->right, right->down, bottom->left, left->up; stop when packed